                        ],
                        "form": "dépaysante"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1e9104f8-0daf-410d-a130-bb9136e45173",
                        "entry_id": "ad053bd9-2b5e-39bc-9592-fde54180bc9c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "dépaysantes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "44615dcc-90f4-3a6d-ba4b-785fb4825ccf",
                        "entry_id": "ad053bd9-2b5e-39bc-9592-fde54180bc9c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui dépayse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "462eac54-b826-4021-9f7d-0a9682072fc2",
                                "sense_id": "44615dcc-90f4-3a6d-ba4b-785fb4825ccf",
                                "text": "Partir en voyage, c'est dépaysant. Ça change du quotidien. Cette situation est différente de mon quotidien mais de manière positive."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47eacee1-f80f-4cc8-9396-771517597f15",
                                "sense_id": "44615dcc-90f4-3a6d-ba4b-785fb4825ccf",
                                "text": "Ne pas aller au bureau pour aller se promener tranquillement en ville, c'est dépaysant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a859fbe-fbf8-4dea-9bef-85893f25961b",
                                "sense_id": "44615dcc-90f4-3a6d-ba4b-785fb4825ccf",
                                "text": "Leur voix psalmodiante et aiguë du grand air et des places vides détonait soudain de façon si dépaysante dans l’indifférence sceptique de ces murs nus qu’ils s’arrêtaient presque aussitôt d’eux-mêmes et se rencoignaient, la tête dans les épaules, comme des oiseaux de nuit, apeurés et chagrins affolés par le son de leur propre voix, tremblants comme un gibier pris au piège."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6494eb52-8194-4e4f-8bc6-7bd49cf2108b",
                        "source_entry_id": "ad053bd9-2b5e-39bc-9592-fde54180bc9c",
                        "source_sense_id": "44615dcc-90f4-3a6d-ba4b-785fb4825ccf",
                        "target_lang_word": "outlandish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "outlandish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1201b5b-6fab-3f16-b3ea-87dfa15529b7",
                                        "entry_id": "53fdd771-014a-344f-a169-9b28ec44f75b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or from a foreign country; not indigenous or native; alien, foreign."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b9bd25d-b3a9-4890-a9f8-390b7c872ea4",
                                                "sense_id": "d1201b5b-6fab-3f16-b3ea-87dfa15529b7",
                                                "text": "[W]e haue bꝛokẽ thy ſtatutes ⁊ cõmaundementes agayne, ⁊ mengled o^ꝛ ſelues wᵗ the vnclẽnes of the outlandiſh heithen.",
                                                "translation": "[W]e have broken thy statutes and commandments again, and mingled ourselves with the uncleanness of the foreign heathen.",
                                                "english": "[W]e have broken thy statutes and commandments again, and mingled ourselves with the uncleanness of the foreign heathen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da8e855e-1e56-4609-b735-d07fb4d0f870",
                                                "sense_id": "d1201b5b-6fab-3f16-b3ea-87dfa15529b7",
                                                "text": "Apiſhneſſe rides in a Chariot made of nothing but cages, in which are all the ſtrangeſt out-landiſh Birds that can be gotten: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35cd72ef-376c-4498-8684-9374b09b385f",
                                                "sense_id": "d1201b5b-6fab-3f16-b3ea-87dfa15529b7",
                                                "text": "Did not Solomon king of Iſrael ſinne by these things? yet among many nations was there no king like him, who was beloued of his God, and God made him king ouer all Iſrael: neuertheleſſe, euen him did outlandiſh women cauſe to ſinne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc1544fd-3b19-4c99-a6d7-d96b03d91c8b",
                                                "sense_id": "d1201b5b-6fab-3f16-b3ea-87dfa15529b7",
                                                "text": "The people therefore of the fair made a great gazing upon them: Some ſaid they vvere Fools, ſome they vvere Bedlams, and ſome they are Outlandiſh-men."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51f8af49-e2b9-418e-96fa-a8d78ba1d4c5",
                                                "sense_id": "d1201b5b-6fab-3f16-b3ea-87dfa15529b7",
                                                "text": "[H]e did not like the name of the outlandish man with the golden clock in his stockings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "480380df-7ebf-40df-8287-c87863038d91",
                                                "sense_id": "d1201b5b-6fab-3f16-b3ea-87dfa15529b7",
                                                "text": "[I]f breeding amongſt Chriſtians vvas as much encouraged as amongſt Dogs and Horſes, vve need not be making Lavvs to let in a Parcel of outlandiſh Locuſts to eat us all up."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e49ea99b-80f4-400e-8b7c-21f02b461247",
                                                "sense_id": "d1201b5b-6fab-3f16-b3ea-87dfa15529b7",
                                                "text": "Slightly observant of the smoky lights; of the people, pipe in mouth, playing with limp cards and yellow dominoes; of the one bare-breasted, bare-armed, soot-begrimed workman reading a journal aloud, and of the others listening to him; of the weapons worn, or laid aside to be resumed; of the two or three customers fallen forward asleep, who in the popular, high-shouldered shaggy black spencer looked, in that attitude, like slumbering bears or dogs; the two outlandish customers approached the counter, and showed what they wanted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e0f3e8dc-3758-3335-8dbb-914334aa5c02",
                                        "entry_id": "53fdd771-014a-344f-a169-9b28ec44f75b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Appearing to be foreign; strange, unfamiliar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df286d3a-c8ea-43dc-adb4-725be9036752",
                                                "sense_id": "e0f3e8dc-3758-3335-8dbb-914334aa5c02",
                                                "text": "I believe, Lady, your Ladyſhip obſerved a young VVoman at Church yeſterday at Even-ſong, vvho vvas dreſt in one of your outlandiſh Garments; I think I have ſeen your Ladyſhip in ſuch a one. Hovvever, in the Country, ſuch Dreſſes are / Rara avis in Terris, nigroq; ſimillima Cycno, / That is, Madam, as much to ſay, / A rare Bird upon the Earth, and very like a black Svvan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "355b5760-285c-4c4b-b3db-cdabe00abfcb",
                                                "sense_id": "e0f3e8dc-3758-3335-8dbb-914334aa5c02",
                                                "text": "Roast beef and plum pudding are also held in superstitious veneration, and port and sherry maintain their grounds as the only true English wines; all others being considered vile outlandish beverages."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79e4650e-2719-35b3-a8b8-4668ca8bfb94",
                                        "entry_id": "53fdd771-014a-344f-a169-9b28ec44f75b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Greatly different from common experience; bizarre, outrageous, strange."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67e55f28-0c38-4746-ba5e-c9ddd6d4bd31",
                                                "sense_id": "79e4650e-2719-35b3-a8b8-4668ca8bfb94",
                                                "text": "The rock star wore black with outlandish pink and green spiked hair."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a315786-b2c1-4d5d-9065-01273e645f83",
                                                "sense_id": "79e4650e-2719-35b3-a8b8-4668ca8bfb94",
                                                "text": "[T]hoſe Laſciuious, Immodeſt, VVhoriſh, or vngodly Faſhions, and Attires, vvhich Metamorphiſe, and Transforme, our Light, and Giddie Females of the Superior and Gentile ranke, into ſundry Antique, Horred, and Out-landiſh ſhapes, from day, to day: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52df304d-92b5-49c6-a86a-319c9aaab69e",
                                                "sense_id": "79e4650e-2719-35b3-a8b8-4668ca8bfb94",
                                                "text": "He was an outlandish figure, with his wide-brimmed hat and pointed beard, among those country folk, and it was easy to see that they thought him very queer; but his spirits were so high, his enthusiasm so contagious, that it was impossible not to like him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5265d9e8-6133-4b9e-bddc-183d1065a12c",
                                                "sense_id": "79e4650e-2719-35b3-a8b8-4668ca8bfb94",
                                                "text": "Except for an eye-catching sky-blue container boldly and attractively featuring the B.T.C.'s \"door-to-door\" arrow symbol[…], there were no outlandish colour schemes or lettering styles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc11258a-49aa-40a6-898f-daa2c11c859c",
                                                "sense_id": "79e4650e-2719-35b3-a8b8-4668ca8bfb94",
                                                "text": "I hardly need to add that this story requires outlandish assumptions to make investment behaviour more passive than one would expect it to be in an industrial capitalist economy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f7f5d823-48c3-3324-81c5-e0753595d5e3",
                                        "entry_id": "53fdd771-014a-344f-a169-9b28ec44f75b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a place: far away from where most people are located; in the middle of nowhere, out of the way, remote."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db5c1fb4-702f-4980-a6f1-07a3ece5f1bc",
                                                "sense_id": "f7f5d823-48c3-3324-81c5-e0753595d5e3",
                                                "text": "It will be very convenient to have a medical man—if he is clever—in one's own parish. I get dreadfully nervous sometimes, living in such an outlandish place; and Sherton is so far to send to."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6766593-a8fe-4e55-a198-b781160df823",
                                                "sense_id": "f7f5d823-48c3-3324-81c5-e0753595d5e3",
                                                "text": "I will take this occasion of adding that we are both enjoying ourselves in these outlandish parts, and only wish for the presence of our friends (yourself and John, to wit) to make the trip perfectly enjoyable as it promises to be instructive."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "outlandish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6257ac1-8bc7-325f-82e2-b229b507dce3",
                                        "entry_id": "c0f152bd-8627-3925-81a6-e7dd4fb89c5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A foreign language."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cd9051d-ae31-41e7-983f-618c05ca0169",
                                                "sense_id": "d6257ac1-8bc7-325f-82e2-b229b507dce3",
                                                "text": "[H]ow soon God from Heaven had sent His fiery tongues upon His Apostles, the devil from hell presently sent for his fiery tongues, and put them in the mouths of his apostles, to disgrace and scoff at those of God's sending. […] These good fellows have been at it, and now they can speak nothing but outlandish. Some little broken Greek or Latin they had, and now out it comes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85452137-8c64-4c0b-83df-d0d78e1c4093",
                                                "sense_id": "d6257ac1-8bc7-325f-82e2-b229b507dce3",
                                                "text": "Never ſtir if that Gentleman ben't the ſame that vve ſee'd at the Painting Man's, that vvas ſo zivil to Mother, only he has got a black VVig on, and ſpeaks outlandiſh."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
